# API Controller Conventions

## Controller Setup (Mandatory)

Controllers MUST implement their corresponding `*Api` interface for OpenAPI documentation.

```java
@Slf4j
@RestController
@RequestMapping(path = "/api/bff/containers", produces = MediaType.APPLICATION_JSON_VALUE)
@Validated
@RequiredArgsConstructor
public class ContainerSearchController implements ContainerSearchApi {
    private final Dispatcher dispatcher;
}
```

**Required annotations:**
- `@RestController` - REST controller
- `@RequestMapping` - Base path with produces
- `@Validated` - Enable method-level validation
- `@RequiredArgsConstructor` - Constructor injection via Lombok

## OpenAPI Documentation Pattern (Mandatory)

> **API documentation MUST be defined in interfaces, NOT in controllers.**

This separation keeps controllers clean and provides a single source of truth for API documentation.

### Step 1: Create API Interface (in web/api/)

```java
@Tag(name = "Container Search", description = "Operations for searching containers")
public interface ContainerSearchApi {
    @Operation(summary = "Search containers by number")
    @ApiResponses({
        @ApiResponse(responseCode = "200", description = "Search completed successfully"),
        @ApiResponse(responseCode = "400", description = "Invalid request"),
        @ApiResponse(responseCode = "503", description = "Backend unavailable")
    })
    ResponseEntity<ContainerSearchResponse> searchContainers(
        @Parameter(description = "Backend system") ExternalApiProvider backend,
        @Parameter(description = "Container number") String containerNumber,
        @Parameter(description = "Trade type") String tradeTypeCode);
}
```

### Step 2: Controller Implements Interface (Clean)

```java
@Slf4j
@RestController
@RequestMapping(path = "/api/bff/containers", produces = MediaType.APPLICATION_JSON_VALUE)
@Validated
@RequiredArgsConstructor
public class ContainerSearchController implements ContainerSearchApi {
    private final Dispatcher dispatcher;

    @Override
    @GetMapping("/search/{backend}")
    public ResponseEntity<ContainerSearchResponse> searchContainers(
            @PathVariable ExternalApiProvider backend,
            @RequestParam("q") String rawContainerNumber,
            @RequestParam(value = "tradeType", defaultValue = "I") String tradeTypeCode) {
        // Business logic only - no OpenAPI annotations
    }
}
```

### Benefits

| Benefit | Description |
|---------|-------------|
| Clean controllers | Controllers contain only business logic |
| Single source of truth | API docs defined in one place |
| Contract-first design | Interface defines the API contract |
| Swagger UI works | Full OpenAPI support |

### File Organization

```
web/
  api/                          # OpenAPI documentation interfaces
    ContainerSearchApi.java     # @Tag, @Operation, @ApiResponses
    AuthApi.java
  controller/                   # Clean controllers (implement interfaces)
    ContainerSearchController.java
    AuthController.java
  dto/                          # Request/Response DTOs
```

## Controller Constraints (Enforced by ArchUnit)

| Allowed | Not Allowed |
|---------|-------------|
| Dispatcher | *Handler directly |
| InputSanitizer | *Port interfaces |
| Request/Response DTOs | *Client (HTTP clients) |
| Domain enums | RestClient |
| Custom validators | Business logic |
| *Api interfaces | OpenAPI annotations directly |

## Conventions Summary

- Controller implements corresponding *Api interface
- NO OpenAPI annotations in controllers (only in *Api interfaces)
- Return ResponseEntity<T> for explicit status codes
- Use @Valid for request body validation
- Sanitize ALL user input before processing
- Use ProblemDetail (RFC 7807) for all error responses
- Controllers are thin - dispatch and transform only
- Log requests at INFO level, details at DEBUG level

